  "id": "MP-CHANGE-2026-0604-044",
  "title": "Fix dependency atlas import edges",
  "version_target": "2026.06.04.001",
  "status": "complete",
  "type": "bugfix",
  "risk_level": "low",
  "date_started": "2026-06-04",
  "date_completed": "2026-06-04",
  "summary": "Restored dependency-atlas local import edge detection after the src/mediapipeline namespace migration, made direct script execution self-bootstrap source imports, and made the maintenance route pass an explicit source PYTHONPATH to the module-mode generator.",
  "reason": "The atlas generator indexed modules but discarded every local import because it compared the first import segment, mediapipeline, to package roots such as mediapipeline.core. The generated atlas therefore reported zero module/domain edges and lost the dependency map.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "maintenance",
    "tooling"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Dependency atlas generation reported 547 modules but 0 module edges and 0 domain edges. Direct script execution without PYTHONPATH crashed before the intended Graphviz error, and the maintenance route depended on inherited API-process PYTHONPATH.",
  "behavior_after": "Dependency atlas generation resolves mediapipeline namespace imports again, reports nonzero module/domain edges, cleans stale atlas files more robustly, direct script execution reaches actionable errors, and the maintenance route prefixes workspace src in the child PYTHONPATH.",
